\"initial_zero_setting_plus_dead_load\": \"≤ 234 g\", \"maximum_weighing_pan_size\": \"Ø 90 mm\"},\n   {\"model\": \"BC-EB/BC-AB\", ..., \"max\": \"50 g - 220 g\", ..., \"n\": \"≤ 220 000\", ..., temp1 \"+17 °C / +27 °C\", temp2 \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", cap \"264 g\", init \"≤ 214 g\", pan \"Ø 90 mm\"},\n   {\"model\": \"BC-EB/BC-AB (class II)\", \"accuracy_class\": \"II\", \"max\": \"0.1 g - 100 g\", \"e\": \"1 mg - 2 mg\", \"d\": \"0.1 mg - 2 mg\", \"n\": \"≤ 100 000\", temp1 \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", temp2 \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", cap \"264 g\", init \"≤ 263 g\", pan \"Ø 90 mm\"}\n ],\n \"footnotes\": [\"1) Only for weighing instruments with incorporated span adjustment device being automatically released.\", \"2) The sum of Max, initial zero setting range and dead load shall not exceed the nominal load of the load receptor.\"]\n}\n\nWait, source Max uses \"–\" en dash sometimes: \"500 g – 1 500 g\", \"0.01 g – 0.1 g\", \"0.001 g – 0.1 g\". I'll normalize to \"-\". Fine.\n\nTable 2:\n{\n \"name\": \"Metrological characteristics (BC-EC/BC-AC, BC-ED/BC-AD)\",\n \"columns\": [same as table 1],\n \"rows\": [\n   {\"model\": \"BC-EC/BC-AC\", \"accuracy_class\": \"I\", \"max\": \"500 g - 1500 g\", \"e\": \"10 mg - 20 mg\", \"d\": \"1 mg - 20 mg\", \"n\": \"≤ 150 000\", \"tare_balancing_range\": \"until 100% of Max\", \"temperature_range_1\": \"+17 °C / +27 °C\", \"temperature_range_2\": \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", \"nominal_capacity_of_load_receptor\": \"1800 g\", \"initial_zero_setting_plus_dead_load\": \"≤ 1300 g\", \"maximum_weighing_pan_size\": \"Ø 120 mm\"},\n   {\"model\": \"BC-ED/BC-AD\", \"accuracy_class\": \"II\", \"max\": \"1 g - 650 g\", \"e\": \"0.01 g - 0.1 g\", \"d\": \"0.001 g - 0.1 g\", \"n\": \"≤ 65 000\", \"temperature_range_1\": \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", \"temperature_range_2\": \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", \"cap\": \"780 g\", \"init\": \"≤ 779 g\", \"pan\": \"Ø 120 mm\"}\n ],\n \"footnotes\": [1), 2)]\n}\n\nTable 3:\n{\n \"name\": \"Metrological characteristics (BC-EE/BC-AE, BC-EF/BC-AF)\",\n \"columns\": [\"model\", \"accuracy_class\", \"max\", \"e\", \"d\", \"n\", \"tare_balancing_range\", \"temperature_range_1\", \"nominal_capacity_of_load_receptor\", \"initial_zero_setting_plus_dead_load\", \"maximum_weighing_pan_size\"],\n \"rows\": [\n  {\"model\": \"BC-EE/BC-AE\", \"accuracy_class\": \"II\", \"max\": \"500 g - 6200 g\", \"e\": \"0.1 g - 1 g\", \"d\": \"0.01 g - 1 g\", \"n\": \"≤ 62 000\", \"tare\": \"until 100% of Max\", \"temperature_range_1\": \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", \"cap\": \"7440 g\", \"init\": \"6940 g\", \"pan\": \"180 mm x 180 mm\"},\n  {\"model\": \"BC-EF/BC-AF\", ..., \"pan\": \"Ø 180 mm\"}\n ],\n \"footnotes\": [\"2) ...\"]\n}\n\nTable 4:\n{\n \"name\": \"Metrological characteristics (BC-EG/BC-AG, BC-EH/BC-AH)\",\n \"columns\": [\"model\", \"accuracy_class\", \"max\", \"e\", \"d\", \"n\", \"tare_balancing_range\", \"temperature_range\", \"nominal_capacity_of_load_receptor\", \"initial_zero_setting_plus_dead_load\", \"maximum_weighing_pan_size\"],\n \"rows\": [\n  {\"model\": \"BC-EG/BC-AG\", \"accuracy_class\": \"II\", \"max\": \"5000 g - 12200 g\", \"e\": \"1 g\", \"d\": \"0.1 g - 1 g\", \"n\": \"≤ 12 200\", \"temperature_range\": \"+10 °C / +30 °C\", \"cap\": \"14640 g\", \"init\": \"≤ 9640 g\", \"pan\": \"180 mm x 180 mm\"},\n  {\"model\": \"BC-EH/BC-AH\", ..., \"pan\": \"Ø 180 mm\"}\n ],\n \"footnotes\": [\"2) ...\"]\n}\n\nI should use full column names in rows (not \"e\" shorthand) for consistency. Yes, use the same keys as columns.\n\nNow double-check numbers once more from markdown:\n\nTable 1:\n- Max: \"50 g - 320 g\" ✓, \"50 g - 220 g\" ✓, \"0,1 g - 100 g\" → 0.1–100 ✓\n- e: 1–2 mg ×3 ✓\n- d: 0.1–2 mg ×3 ✓\n- n: ≤320 000, ≤220 000, ≤100 000 ✓\n- Temp1: +17/+27, +17/+27, +10/+30 ✓\n- Temp2: +10/+30 ×3 (fn1) ✓\n- Nom cap: 384, 264, 264 ✓\n- Init: ≤234, ≤214, ≤263 (fn2) ✓\n- Pan: Ø90 ×3 ✓\n\nTable 2:\n- EC/AC: I, Max 500–1500, e 10–20 mg, d 1–20 mg, n ≤150 000, T1 +17/+27, T2 +10/+30, cap 1 800 g, init ≤1300 g, pan Ø120 ✓\n- ED/AD: II, Max 1–650 g, e 0.01–0.1 g, d 0.001–0.1 g, n ≤65 000, T1 +10/+30, T2 +10/+30, cap 780, init ≤779, pan Ø120 ✓\n\nTable 3:\n- EE/AE: II, Max 500–6200, e 0.1–1 g, d 0.01–1 g, n ≤62 000, T1 +10/+30 (colspan), cap 7 440, init 6 940 (no ≤), pan 180×180 ✓\n- EF/AF: same, pan Ø180 ✓\n\nTable 4:\n- EG/AG: II, Max 5000–12200, e 1 g, d 0.1–1 g, n ≤12 200, Temp +10/+30, cap 14 640, init ≤9 640, pan 180×180 ✓\n- EH/AH: same, pan Ø180 ✓\n\nAll good.\n\nRecommendation: \"OIML R 76-1, edition 2006\" → id \"R76\", edition 2006. accuracy_classes [\"I\",\"II\"] from \"( I ), ( II )\".\n\nNow certificate page_total: 4 (\"1/4\"..\"4/4\").\n\nAlso project_number — omit.\n\nOne more check: \"Conformity Evaluation Body METAS-Cert\" — maybe include in issuing_authority as part of name? I'll include name as \"Federal Institute of Metrology METAS\" and add address line? No — better to keep person_title. Fine.\n\nFinal JSON assembly. Ensure no markdown fences. Also decide: include \"components\" — no, omit (none). Include \"amendment\": omit.\n\nFootnote markers format: source uses \"1)\" and \"2)\". Use those markers consistently in footnotes[] and footnote_markers.\n\nLet me write the final JSON.",
